ostdraft_citation_weave_agent_codex_20261113_180124.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   84007 Nov 13 19:00 postdraft_citation_weave_prompt.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    6364 Nov 13 18:57 postdraft_reference_query_plan.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    7827 Nov 13 18:57 postdraft_reference_query_plan.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent  239640 Nov 13 18:58 postdraft_reference_query_plan_agent_codex_20261113_180124.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    2559 Nov 13 18:54 postdraft_reference_query_plan_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov 13 18:58 postdraft_reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     279 Nov 13 18:58 postdraft_reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    3411 Nov 13 19:00 postdraft_reference_retrieval.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    7615 Nov 13 18:27 postdraft_references.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   40608 Nov 13 18:27 postdraft_references_provenance.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   29226 Nov 13 19:08 reference_consultation.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     657 Nov 13 19:08 reference_consultation.md.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    8542 Nov 13 18:05 reference_query_plan.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   10892 Nov 13 18:05 reference_query_plan.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 1260096 Nov 13 18:05 reference_query_plan_agent_codex_20261113_180124.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   35543 Nov 13 18:01 reference_query_plan_prompt.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov 13 18:05 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     279 Nov 13 18:05 reference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    3398 Nov 13 18:08 reference_retrieval.log\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    8223 Nov 13 19:07 references.bib\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     683 Nov 13 19:08 references.bib.prov.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    7615 Nov 13 18:58 references.pre_postdraft.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   40608 Nov 13 18:58 references.pre_postdraft.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   43451 Nov 13 19:08 references_provenance.json\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent      16 Nov 13 18:01 results -> ../investigation\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    3716 Nov 13 18:27 retrieve_vetted_references.py\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 agent agent    4096 Nov 13 19:16 scientific-evidence\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 agent agent    4096 Nov 13 18:48 source_evidence\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     265 Nov 13 18:19 strategy_validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     271 Nov 13 18:19 strategy_validation_feedback.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 agent agent    4096 Nov 13 18:44 tables\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 agent agent       7 Nov 13 18:01 task -> ../task\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    2608 Nov 13 19:16 validation_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    1814 Nov 13 19:16 validation_feedback.md\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   16645 Nov 13 19:16 validation_report.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    4860 Nov 13 18:46 verify_paper_artifacts.py\n--- VENUE.md\n# ICLR 2026 Venue Brief\n\nUse this brief to tailor the manuscript for the International Conference on Learning\nRepresentations 2026 submission.\n\n## Hard Constraints\n- Target venue: ICLR 2026.\n- Submission type: conference paper.\n- Body-page budget: 8 to 9 pages, excluding references. A body of 8 pages counts only when its final page is at least 75% full; a shorter or sparser body fails validation.\n- Review model: double-blind. The submission must be fully anonymized.\n- Omit author names, affiliations, acknowledgements, and funding statements from the manuscript.\n- Do not include self-identifying links such as personal repositories, lab pages, or internal URLs.\n- Refer to your own prior work in the third person; never write phrasing that reveals authorship.\n- Include a separate `LLM Usage` section, which may appear in the appendix, describing the precise role\n  of LLMs in research ideation and writing. Significant LLM use must be disclosed; nondisclosure can\n  cause desk rejection.\n- The paper must satisfy the ICLR template and formatting rules selected by `--paper-format iclr`.\n\n## Audience\n- Machine learning researchers working on representation learning, optimization, architectures, and\n  empirical methodology.\n- Readers expect a clearly stated contribution, honest baselines, controlled comparisons, ablations\n  that isolate the mechanism, and explicit statements of scope and limitations.\n- Reviewers reward reproducibility and calibrated claims far more than headline numbers.\n\n## Framing Priorities\n- Lead with the research question and the specific claim the evidence supports.\n- State the contribution precisely in the abstract and introduction: what is new, what it improves,\n  and under which conditions.\n- Motivate the method mechanistically. Explain why it should work, not only that it does.\n- Support the central claim with controlled comparisons against meaningful baselines.\n- Use ablations to attribute the gain to the proposed component rather than to incidental changes.\n- Report variance across seeds or runs whenever the artifacts provide it.\n- Be explicit about the regime studied and where the result is not expected to hold.\n\n## Manuscript Guidance\n- Prefer a title and abstract that name the mechanism and the setting, not a generic improvement claim.\n- In the introduction, make the contribution list concrete and verifiable against the artifacts.\n- In the method section, give enough detail to reimplement: objective, architecture, and the\n  hyperparameters that matter.\n- In the results section, foreground controlled comparisons, ablations, sensitivity, and failure modes.\n- Include a limitations discussion that a reviewer would otherwise raise.\n- Figures must meet top-tier conference standards in both design (clean typography, consistent colors,\n  proper labels and legends, high resolution) and scientific content (clear message, no filler).\n- The template is single-column: size figures for the full text width and keep axis labels legible.\n\n## Anti-Goals\n- Do not deanonymize the submission in any way.\n- Do not overclaim generality beyond the settings actually evaluated.\n- Do not present a benchmark delta as a mechanistic insight without evidence connecting the two.\n- Do not omit baselines or ablations that the grounded artifacts already support.\n- Do not describe results as state of the art unless the comparison in the artifacts establishes it.\n- Do not pad the paper to fill the page budget.\n\n## Decision Rule\n- When venue framing and grounded evidence conflict, follow the grounded evidence.\n- Use this brief to choose emphasis, terminology, and narrative framing, not to invent stronger claims\n  than the run supports.\n--- validation_feedback.json\n{\n  \"agentic_evidence_audit\": {\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"finding_count\": 0,\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"summary\": \"Main-text and supplementary claims match the grounded evidence and preserve failed qualification, missing-output limitations, and conditional comparison scope.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"pass\"\n  },\n  \"evidence_validation\": {\n    \"bundle_path\": \"work/results/t07/codex/20261113_154315/paper/scientific-evidence\",\n    \"bundle_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"dangling\": [],\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"paper_token_count\": 188,\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"anchored_references\": 113,\n      \"dangling_references\": 0,\n      \"manifests_checked\": 17,\n      \"resolved_references\": 75,\n      \"total_references\": 188\n    },\n    \"verification_report_path\": \"work/results/t07/codex/20261113_154315/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\"\n  },\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-13T19:16:14.093055+00:00\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [\n    \"figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for available_pair_method_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for budget_accuracy_and_ranking\"\n  ],\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"page_validation\": {\n    \"body_pages\": null,\n    \"checked\": false,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"exclud